<title>NEW ZEALAND: Ceramco year net profit slips 91 percent.</title>
<headline>Ceramco year net profit slips 91 percent.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year result to March 31</p>
<p>			   (million NZ$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			   0.96 vs 11.3</p>
<p>    Div (cents)			   7.5 vs same</p>
<p>    Total div (cents)		   7.5 vs 17.5</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)				 1.99 vs 23.35</p>
<p>    Turnover				   96.07 vs 104.3</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			     4.71 vs 7.46</p>
<p>    Abnormals			   debit 3.26 vs 6.29 credit</p>
<p>    Tax					   0.49 vs 2.34</p>
<p>    Shares outstanding (million)	  48.5 vs same</p>
<p>Dividend carries full imputation credits.</p>
<p>Pay date June 27</p>
<p>Reg date June 13</p>
<p>    Ex div   June 16</p>
<p>Note - Ceramco Corp Ltd is an apparel and ceramics manufacturer. Previous year's profit was inflated by a NZ$6.54 million non-recurring profit arising from the sale of the company's stake in Baycorp Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Wellington newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
